## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design a privacy-preserving, multi-tenant AI workflow at scale, with strict data isolation, governance, and measurable latency.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant OpenAI deployment and prompt routing
- Real-time ingestion (Event Hubs) and low-latency scoring
- KB grounding via Cognitive Search on Blob data
- PII redaction (Text Analytics) and per-tenant masking (Key Vault)
- RBAC (Azure AD), Data Lake auditing, canary rollout

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: route prompt for tenant, redact, ground, respond
async function handleRequest(req){
  const tenantId = req.headers['x-tenant'];
  const raw = req.body;
  const redacted = redactPII(raw);
  const kb = loadKBVersion(tenantId);
  const prompt = buildPrompt(redacted, kb, tenantId);
  const resp = await openai.complete(prompt, {deployment: getDeployment(tenantId)});
  logAudit(tenantId, prompt, resp);
  return resp;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How to quantify latency vs. isolation trade-offs?
- How to implement drift detection for the KB and prompts across tenants?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design secure, scalable, multi-tenant AI-assisted incident triage on Azure with data governance.

## Key Concepts

- Retrieval-augmented generation
- Multi-tenant RBAC and data isolation
- PII redaction and compliance
- Canary deployment and rollback
- Audit logs and data lake

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode sketch of flow stages
async function handleEvent(e) {
  const norm = normalize(e);
  const doc = await kbQuery(norm, tenantId);
  const prompt = buildPrompt(doc, norm);
  const resp = await openai.infer(prompt);
  const safe = redact(resp);
  await logAudit({tenantId, event: e, resp: safe});
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the sandboxing to prevent prompt injection in a CI/CD pipeline?
- Which metrics and SLAs would you monitor to ensure per-tenant quota enforcement doesn't throttle critical alerts?
